{
  "description": "Golden category table (issue #39; corrected in PR #50 review for the combo side-slot pricing regression): every menuItems.json entry mapped to two INDEPENDENT fields -- comboSlot (sides|drinks|none: can this item fill a combo's included side/drink slot for free) and happyHourDiscounted (true|false: does this item get the happy-hour discount). These are deliberately separate columns, not one shared bucket (PR #50 review) -- a future change to one must not silently change the other. size/unitPrice (quoted exact-decimal strings, matching golden-order-pricing.json's money convention -- PR #50 review cheap follow-up) are the representative (Medium, else Standard, else first-listed) size/price from menuItems.json used by the C# combo-absorption Theory (GoldenMenuComboSlotTheoryTests.cs) -- not a pricing contract on their own. Source of truth: app/backend/menu_utils.py::infer_combo_component (comboSlot) and ::is_happy_hour_discounted (happyHourDiscounted). comboSlot=\"sides\" is an explicit allow-list of exactly Tots and Groovy Fries -- the menu's own combo description says \"your choice of a side (Tots or Fries) and a drink\" -- NOT the whole Hot Dogs & Tots / Extras & Sides JSON category (that wider mapping was the PR #50 pricing regression: 9+ items were being silently absorbed for free into a combo's side slot). comboSlot=\"drinks\" is unchanged from dev: every Slushes & Drinks item, plus every Shakes & Ice Cream item except the two sundaes (Hot Fudge Sundae, Caramel Sundae -- Brian's #39 decision: full price during happy hour, not a combo drink either). happyHourDiscounted mirrors comboSlot==\"drinks\" today except it is derived independently in code -- Shakes & Ice Cream (minus sundaes) is currently discounted pending Brian's ruling (see menu_utils._SHAKES_AND_BLASTS_HAPPY_HOUR_DISCOUNTED, a single flag so his eventual answer is a one-line change). Hot-dog entrees (All-American Dog, Chili Cheese Coney, Footlong Quarter Pound Coney, Corn Dog) are comboSlot=none/happyHourDiscounted=false -- real food items, not a fillable combo slot, despite sharing the Hot Dogs & Tots JSON category with Tots and Groovy Fries.",
